{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' aristotle_tasks/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem.md && printf '\\\\n--- decision ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,240p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- P49 closeout ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md && printf '\\\\n--- P49A closeout ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,300p' reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md && printf '\\\\n--- status/progress context ---\\\\n' && for f in PROGRESS.md STATUS.md HANDOFF.md work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md; do [ -f \\\"\"'$f\" ] && { printf '\"'\\\\n### %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$f\"; }; done'","aggregated_output":"# P49B — analytic von Neumann bicommutant theorem\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1269-1287`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P49B`; Lane `shared` analytic infrastructure used by G.\n- **Predecessors:** `P49A`, integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** prove that the bicommutant of a represented unital\n  complex star algebra is its strong-operator closure.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no Kaplansky unit-ball density, no corner\n  trace, no normality/faithfulness conclusion, no finiteness/fullness, and no\n  factor classification.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean`. For a\nunital complex star subalgebra `A ⊆ B(H)`, prove both inclusions and the equality\n\n`strongOperatorClosure A = A''`.\n\nDevelop the missing proof locally. A permissible route is the standard\nfinite-amplification argument: simultaneous approximation on finitely many\nvectors, the cyclic subspace generated by the diagonal amplification of `A`,\nits orthogonal projection in the amplified commutant, and invariance under an\noperator in `A''`. The theorem must cover arbitrary finite strong neighborhoods,\nnot merely sequential closure or one-vector approximation.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nState the exact unitality/nondegeneracy hypotheses genuinely used. The central\nequality must be proved from them. It may not be represented by a structure\nfield, postulate, external-theorem token, or new axiom.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean`. Import P49A\nand the algebraic bicommutant core. Necessary finite direct-sum/amplification\nsupporting definitions may live in this owned module. Do not import P49C or P50.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem` succeeds.\n- The strong-closure/bicommutant equality is an actual Lean theorem and handles\n  nets/finite strong neighborhoods, not only sequences.\n- No forbidden declaration or supplied replacement of the theorem occurs.\n- If more local topology is required, develop it in the owned module. If the\n  theorem remains unproved, halt and report the minimal remaining lemma graph.\n\n--- decision ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\n--- P49 closeout ---\n# P49 closeout review — finite-stage trace and compressed quasi-local corner\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: partial; queue must halt.**\n\nThe Aristotle result contains a technically sound-looking, conditional candidate\nmodule, but it is not accepted or integrated.  The packet's required source\ndeclaration is `main.tex:1196-1335`, while the candidate explicitly attributes\nits finite-stage cyclicity and codespace-density identities to the manuscript.\nThose identities occur at `main.tex:1133-1191`: in particular, the vector\nfixing calculation is at lines 1133-1148, the functional is stated at\n1150-1158, and finite-stage cyclicity and `eq:local_traciality` are at\n1161-1191.  Lines 1196-1335 begin only with the bounded strong-limit passage\nand then the C-star and von Neumann extensions.  Thus the packet does not give\nthe exact source locator required for all of its manuscript-derived claims.\n\nChanging the packet or candidate locator would be a scope/policy edit outside\nthis bounded closeout.  The candidate remains only in the response quarantine;\nthe live working tree was not given `AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean`.\n\nThe downloaded raw response record is\n`aristotle_responses/P49-finite-corner-trace.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`17ceca9683eb286ebd136fb5fc2238f97fb077f2d1f73dacff93ff548ebe5473`), extracted\nwithout a build, update, or dependency fetch at\n`aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle/`.\nIts candidate module has SHA-256\n`38d4cbb58104d88f9830aa6b73846d6309f497f48b4140f762a2f031343be487`.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions reviewed\n\nThe quarantined module declares, under complex Hilbert-space assumptions, the\nfollowing scoped results:\n\n- `tauVec`, `compressL`, and `cornerTau`, with\n  `cornerTau_star_mul_self`, `cornerTau_nonneg`, `cornerTau_one`, and\n  `compressL_mem_corner`;\n- `trace_density_sandwich_comm`, `stabilizerCodeDensity`,\n  `trace_stabilizerCodeDensity`, `trace_groupAverage_eq`, and\n  `posSemidef_smul_of_isIdempotent`;\n- `FiniteCodespaceSystem`, `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem`, and the derived\n  `FiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj_apply_self`,\n  `FiniteCodespaceSystem.stage_cyclic`, and\n  `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.trace_density_incl`;\n- `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich`, `cornerTau_cyclic_of_stage`,\n  `CornerTracialOn.closure`,\n  `cornerTracialOn_quasilocalCStarAlgebra`, and the packaged conditional\n  theorem `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace`.\n\nThe candidate's named auxiliary data are explicit: finite stage star\nrepresentations; hermitian idempotent code projections; densities of the form\n`weight n • codeProj n` with trace one; the vector-state identity; compatible\nstage inclusions; the P48 decreasing-projection-tower premise; and a\nnorm-density inclusion into the closure of finite-stage ranges.  No normality,\nfaithfulness on the von Neumann corner, fullness, finiteness of `q`, global\nweight, or type-III conclusion is declared.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | In the live project's Lean environment, the quarantined module type-checks.  Its conditional finite-stage/corner-C-star statements compile, and the four sampled key declarations depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. |\n| partial | The Lean result is a conditional finite-stage and norm-closed quasi-local statement, not a proof of a trace on `q M_Gamma q`.  More importantly, its source-backed presentation needs the packet locator expanded to cover `main.tex:1133-1191`; that correction is not made in this closeout. |\n| blocked | Acceptance is blocked by the source-locator mismatch.  P50's separate Kaplansky-density/normality passage remains unaddressed, as required. |\n| failed | No Lean compilation or forbidden-declaration failure was found.  The task fails acceptance solely on the mandatory source-authority/context requirement. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is therefore **not accepted at its stated\nmanuscript-facing scope**, despite the successful conditional Lean check.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49, Lane G — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P47 and P48 are locally integrated and audited.  Their live\n  SHA-256 values match the corresponding files in quarantine:\n  `c55831ac16d3dec3d471c25c24159a5c22c79dff1460c586830eadda27da57d8`\n  (P47) and\n  `190af007e460f439360a0e195c6458e23f0aa5146009cb7f6b40ece2ea6b2386`\n  (P48).\n- **Permitted gate:** the candidate addresses only finite-stage cyclicity and\n  its norm-closed compressed quasi-local extension, with explicit finite\n  codespace density data.  This is the P49 gate.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected in the candidate.  The scan found\n  no theorem asserting normality, faithfulness, finiteness/fullness, a global\n  trace/weight, Kaplansky density, a double-commutant theorem, or central\n  type-III exclusion.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake env lean <quarantined FiniteCornerTrace.lean>` — passed, run from the\n  already-built live project; no build, update, or fetch was run in quarantine.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed.\n- `#print axioms` for `finite_corner_trace`, `stage_cyclic`,\n  `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich`, and `CornerTracialOn.closure` — only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scans of the candidate and its direct\n  project imports — no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`,\n  `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo Lean-term defect was found in the reviewed route: the strong-limit argument\nuses `p_n Omega = Omega` to reduce the product limit to pointwise convergence,\nand the C-star extension uses continuity on the product closure.  The\nacceptance-blocking defect is provenance, not compilation: the declared source\nrange omits the exact finite-stage clauses the candidate claims to formalize.\nCompilation and axiom inspection cannot repair that source mismatch or prove\nthe later von Neumann-algebraic conclusions.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the ignored raw archive and quarantine extraction, for the\nsupervisor's inspection.  Not integrated: `FiniteCornerTrace.lean`.  Preserved\nunchanged: the pre-existing untracked P49A candidate and its closeout review.\nNo manuscript file was changed, and no commit, push, remote submission,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n\n--- P49A closeout ---\n# P49A closeout review — strong-operator closed concrete von Neumann algebras\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256 `eb1bd6ddf17213aaf2ba0062f0fe7ba5b0851f4a46eff6ea655801bb3f70d56e`)\nand extracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49a-p0kpdbli_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` was integrated\ninto the live project. Its SHA-256 is\n`dfb39289d895c16400e05145112320a42e6d1b61736859edbba153d02df0571a`\nin both the quarantine snapshot and live project. The archive and extraction\nremain raw response records. No manuscript file was modified.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `H` with `[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]`, the module\ndefines the SOT synonym `StrongOperator.SOT H`, the pointwise predicate\n`StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto`, and `StrongOperator.IsStronglyClosed`.\nThe exact core theorems are:\n\n- `StrongOperator.stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot` and\n  `StrongOperator.tendsto_sot_iff_forall_tendsto`;\n- `StrongOperator.mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto` and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_centralizer`;\n- under `[CompleteSpace H]`,\n  `StrongOperator.coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer`,\n  `StrongOperator.mem_vonNeumannAlgebra_of_stronglyTendsto`, and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra`;\n- `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.const_mul`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_const`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_bounded`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_norm_le`, and\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.compress`.\n\nThe only analytic assumptions are the standard complex inner-product-space\nstructure, and completeness precisely where Mathlib's concrete\n`VonNeumannAlgebra H` requires it. The joint-product theorem explicitly\nrequires a uniform norm bound on its left family. No analytic conclusion is a\nstructure field or axiom.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | All four packet conclusions are proved: SOT/net equivalence; strong closedness of arbitrary commutants; strong closedness of concrete von Neumann algebras using `M = M''`; and fixed-side plus uniformly bounded joint product stability. |\n| partial | None within the stated P49A infrastructure target. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the stated gate. The analytic double-commutant theorem and Kaplansky density remain separate P49B/P49C work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe mathematical target is met at its stated scope. In particular,\n`isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra` is a closure theorem for an already\ngiven Mathlib concrete von Neumann algebra; it does not identify the strong\nclosure of an arbitrary star subalgebra with its bicommutant.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49A, Lane shared.\n- **Predecessors:** P48 was previously integrated and locally audited. The\n  candidate imports only the locally present supporting module\n  `AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; it imports no P49B, P49C,\n  P50, or later package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: commutants and therefore Mathlib concrete\n  von Neumann algebras are closed under strong-operator limits.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. No double-commutant equality\n  with a strong closure, Kaplansky density, corner trace, faithfulness,\n  finiteness, fullness, or type classification is asserted.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for all four core\n  conclusions and the compression corollary — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate — no executable\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. Search hits occur only\n  in the file's explicit negative-scope documentation.\n- Quarantine/live byte comparison, SHA-256 comparison, and `git diff --check`\n  — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that the centralizer proof\npasses the commutation equation pointwise through the two strong limits; that\nthe concrete von Neumann result uses only its defining bicommutant equality;\nand that the product proof has the required uniform norm bound on the left\nfactor. The remaining risk is exactly the deliberately deferred P49B/P49C\nanalytic identification and density work; compilation and axiom inspection do\nnot establish those results.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P49A candidate, its ignored quarantine\narchive and extraction, and this closeout review. No commit, push, manuscript\nchange, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed\nlocally. The new candidate and review are the only working-tree changes from\nthis closeout.\n\n--- status/progress context ---\n\n### PROGRESS.md\n# Formalization progress\n\n## Context policy (2026-08-05)\n\nAll future manuscript-facing formalization takes its context only from\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, with exact locators in the manuscript `main.tex`. Earlier\ngLU/refinement/layer-coherence artifacts remain available only as explicitly\nlabelled legacy infrastructure; they are not manuscript hypotheses. See\n`AGENTS.md` and `CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`.\n\nThe manuscript-facing module sequence is now `Formalization.Manuscript`:\nsource boundary, finite model, algebraic limit, product state, conditional GNS\nbridge, trace dichotomy, and only then the pending theorem contract. Existing\nimplementation files remain in place and are imported through facades.\n\n- P17 — under a supplied finite adapted-coordinate/word realization, the\n  finite pure/mixed product state is exactly the stabilizer indicator on every\n  supplied source Pauli basis word.\n- P18 — a supplied finite matrix-factor tensor decomposition transports the\n  finite product trace to an algebraic tracial state with its elementary-tensor\n  formula.\n- P19 — a supplied C-star model plus compatible states packages the existing\n  GNS unitary and algebraic commutant transport into one bridge interface.\n- P23 — supplied coherent finite-stage star equivalences induce the infinite\n  algebraic direct-limit regional equivalence `alpha`, with finite-stage and\n  inverse formulas. No C-star or von Neumann extension is claimed.\n- P24 — compatible target-stage algebraic states pull back along `alpha` to a\n  unique algebraic direct-limit state with its exact finite-stage expectation\n  formula and conditional stabilizer-indicator corollary.\n- P25 — supplied C-star completions and an extension of `alpha` yield an\n  isometric continuous C-star equivalence and continuous state pullback;\n  existence of those completions remains an explicit assumption.\n\n## Checked Lean results\n\n- `TPT-001` / `TPT-002` — an algebraic tracial state pulls back along a\n  complex `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- TPT-003 — algebraic traciality is reflected as well as preserved by a\n  complex star-algebra equivalence; hence a nontracial product state cannot\n  become tracial after an algebraic coordinate identification.\n- `FMT-001` — the normalized trace on a nonempty finite full matrix algebra is\n  an algebraic tracial state.  Positivity is proved by the explicit\n  trace-of-a-star-square sum-of-squares identity.\n- `FSC-001` — a finite corner equipped with a star isomorphism to a full matrix\n  algebra inherits that algebraic tracial state.\n- `FTT-001` — the finite algebraic tensor product of two matrix factors is\n  identified by the Kronecker star isomorphism, and its normalized trace\n  factorizes on elementary tensors; tensoring with a matrix identity preserves\n  the trace.\n- `FAM-001` — if `R` has an algebraic tracial state, then its finite matrix\n  amplification `Matrix n n R` has the normalized diagonal tracial state.\n  Positivity is checked as a finite sum of coefficient-algebra star-squares.\n  An explicit `StarAlgEquiv` transports this finite type-I product trace to a\n  target algebra.\n- `TMT-001` — the finite type-I product is now identified canonically, not\n  supplied as an assumption: `Matrix n n ℂ ⊗[ℂ] R` is star-isomorphic to\n  `Matrix n n R`.  Its trace factors on elementary tensors as the normalized\n  matrix trace times the coefficient trace.\n- `DTT-001` — the actual dyadic finite-stage system is constructed as\n  `A₀ = ℂ`, `Aₙ₊₁ = Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Aₙ`, with diagonal identity-qubit\n  embeddings.  Its normalized traces are compatible with every stage map,\n  and their algebraic directed limit carries the induced algebraic tracial\n  state.\n- FPU-001 — for every nonempty finite matrix factor, its algebraic tensor\n  product with the concrete dyadic algebraic limit carries the checked product\n  tracial state.  The theorem includes the elementary-tensor formula\n  tr_p(a) times qubitUHFTrace(u).\n- FPU-002 — any supplied regional `StarAlgEquiv` into that finite-pure\n  product model induces an algebraic tracial state on the regional algebra,\n  with the checked formula on inverse images of elementary tensors.\n- `AIT-001` — compatible unital cyclic finite-stage functionals glue to a\n  unital cyclic linear functional on mathlib's algebraic directed direct\n  limit.\n- `AIT-002` — compatible stagewise star-algebra maps induce an involutive,\n  additive, multiplication-reversing star on that algebraic direct limit.\n  Compatible algebraic tracial states then glue to an ordinary algebraic\n  tracial state there.\n- `SPC-001` — an adapted Hamel basis identifies the label space with finitely\n  supported X/Z coordinate labels and maps the singleton coordinate labels to\n  the chosen basis vectors.\n- ASC-001 — for a selected set of Z coordinates, Lean now identifies the\n  corresponding coordinate subspace both as the span of those Z basis\n  vectors and as the finite words with no X coordinate and no Z coordinate\n  outside the selected set.  This is the exact linear selection criterion\n  required before comparing the regional stabilizer state with the\n  pure/mixed product state.\n- FQS-001 — Lean now reads the recursive finite-qubit Pauli label as its\n  finite X/Z coordinate list and proves that the pure/mixed product-state\n  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n\n### work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n\n### work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
