{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u /dev/null aristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49b-sn5_fvfw_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean | sed '1,2c--- /dev/null\\\\n+++ AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean'\"","aggregated_output":"--- /dev/null\n+++ AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n@@ -0,0 +1,491 @@\n+import Mathlib\n+import AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\n+import AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann\n+\n+/-!\n+# P49B — the analytic von Neumann bicommutant (double commutant) theorem\n+\n+**Infrastructure only.**  This file makes no manuscript claim.  It proves, for an arbitrary\n+complex Hilbert space `H` and an arbitrary star subalgebra `A ⊆ B(H)`, the *analytic* double\n+commutant theorem\n+\n+    strongClosure A = A''  ( = `StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A` ),\n+\n+where `strongClosure` is the closure in the **strong operator topology** and `A''` is the\n+algebraic bicommutant of `AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`.\n+\n+## Plan alignment\n+\n+* **Package and lane:** `P49B`, lane `shared` (analytic infrastructure used by Lane G).\n+* **Predecessors:** `P49A` (`AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann`) and the\n+  algebraic bicommutant core (`AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`), both imported.\n+* **Gate discharged:** the bicommutant of a represented unital complex star algebra equals its\n+  strong-operator closure.\n+* **Forbidden downstream claims, not made here:** no Kaplansky unit-ball density, no corner\n+  trace, no normality or faithfulness statement, no finiteness or fullness, and no factor\n+  classification.\n+\n+## Hypotheses actually used\n+\n+* `H` is a complex inner product space which is **complete** (`[CompleteSpace H]`).  Completeness\n+  is genuinely used: the cyclic subspace has to carry an orthogonal projection, and adjoints of\n+  bounded operators are needed for the invariant-subspace argument.\n+* `A` is a `StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)`.  In Mathlib a `StarSubalgebra` over `ℂ` is in\n+  particular a unital subalgebra, so the **unitality** hypothesis `1 ∈ A` of the classical\n+  statement is automatic and is recorded by `StarSubalgebra.one_mem`; it is used exactly once, to\n+  see that the cyclic vector `ξ` lies in the cyclic subspace generated by `A`.  No further\n+  nondegeneracy assumption is required.\n+\n+No structure field, external token, axiom, `sorry`, `opaque` or `implemented_by` is used: the\n+central equality `strongClosure A = A''` is proved.\n+\n+## Method\n+\n+The nontrivial inclusion `A'' ⊆ strongClosure A` is the standard **finite amplification**\n+argument, developed here from scratch because the pinned Mathlib does not contain it:\n+\n+1. `VonNeumannBicommutant.ampOp` — the diagonal amplification of an operator to\n+   `Amp H n = PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H)`, assembled into a star algebra homomorphism\n+   `VonNeumannBicommutant.ampHom`;\n+2. `VonNeumannBicommutant.commute_starProjection_of_invariant` — if a closed subspace is\n+   invariant under `b` and under `star b`, the orthogonal projection onto it commutes with `b`;\n+3. `VonNeumannBicommutant.ampOp_commute_of_mem_bicommutant` — the matrix-entry computation showing\n+   that `T ∈ A''` implies `ampOp n T ∈ (ampOp n '' A)''`;\n+4. `VonNeumannBicommutant.exists_mem_approx_on_fin` — the resulting simultaneous approximation on\n+   an *arbitrary finite family* of vectors.\n+\n+The strong closure is defined as a genuine topological closure in Mathlib's\n+`PointwiseConvergenceCLM` (= the strong operator topology, as used by `P49A`), so the theorem is a\n+statement about arbitrary finite strong neighbourhoods / nets, not about sequences;\n+`VonNeumannBicommutant.mem_strongClosure_iff` makes the finite-neighbourhood form explicit.\n+-/\n+\n+universe u\n+\n+open Filter Topology ContinuousLinearMap\n+\n+namespace VonNeumannBicommutant\n+\n+/-! ## The strong operator closure of a set of operators -/\n+\n+section StrongClosure\n+\n+variable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n+\n+/-- The **strong operator closure** of a set `K` of bounded operators: the closure of `K` inside\n+`StrongOperator.SOT H`, Mathlib's strong-operator-topologized copy of `H →L[ℂ] H`. -/\n+def strongClosure (K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H) :=\n+  {T | StrongOperator.toSOT T ∈\n+    closure {B : StrongOperator.SOT H | StrongOperator.ofSOT B ∈ K}}\n+\n+theorem subset_strongClosure (K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) : K ⊆ strongClosure K := fun _ hT =>\n+  @subset_closure (StrongOperator.SOT H) _ _ _ hT\n+\n+/-- The strong closure is contained in any strongly closed set containing `K`.  (`P49A`'s\n+`StrongOperator.IsStronglyClosed` is used as the notion of strong closedness.) -/\n+theorem strongClosure_subset {K C : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} (hKC : K ⊆ C)\n+    (hC : StrongOperator.IsStronglyClosed C) : strongClosure K ⊆ C := by\n+  intro T hT\n+  have h : closure {B : StrongOperator.SOT H | StrongOperator.ofSOT B ∈ K}\n+      ⊆ {B : StrongOperator.SOT H | StrongOperator.ofSOT B ∈ C} :=\n+    closure_minimal (fun B hB => hKC hB) hC\n+  exact h hT\n+\n+/-- **Finite-neighbourhood form, sufficiency.**  If `T` can be approximated by elements of `K`\n+simultaneously on every finite set of vectors, then `T` lies in the strong closure of `K`. -/\n+theorem mem_strongClosure_of_approx {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n+    (h : ∀ (F : Finset H) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ∃ a ∈ K, ∀ x ∈ F, ‖T x - a x‖ < ε) :\n+    T ∈ strongClosure K := by\n+  classical\n+  rw [strongClosure, Set.mem_setOf_eq, mem_closure_iff_nhds]\n+  intro U hU\n+  have hind := PointwiseConvergenceCLM.isEmbedding_coeFn (σ := RingHom.id ℂ) (E := H) (F := H)\n+  rw [hind.isInducing.nhds_eq_comap, Filter.mem_comap] at hU\n+  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVU⟩ := hU\n+  rw [nhds_pi, Filter.mem_pi] at hV\n+  obtain ⟨I, hI, t, ht, htV⟩ := hV\n+  have hr : ∀ x : H, ∃ r : ℝ, 0 < r ∧ Metric.ball (T x) r ⊆ t x := fun x =>\n+    Metric.mem_nhds_iff.1 (ht x)\n+  choose r hr0 hrt using hr\n+  set s : Finset H := hI.toFinset with hs\n+  set ε : ℝ := (insert (1 : ℝ) (s.image r)).min' (by simp) with hε\n+  have hε0 : 0 < ε := by\n+    have hmem := Finset.min'_mem (insert (1 : ℝ) (s.image r)) (by simp)\n+    rcases Finset.mem_insert.1 hmem with h1 | h1\n+    · rw [hε, h1]; norm_num\n+    · obtain ⟨x, _, hx⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 h1\n+      rw [hε, ← hx]; exact hr0 x\n+  have hεle : ∀ x ∈ s, ε ≤ r x := fun x hx =>\n+    Finset.min'_le _ _ (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image_of_mem r hx))\n+  obtain ⟨a, haK, ha⟩ := h s ε hε0\n+  refine ⟨StrongOperator.toSOT a, hVU (htV ?_), haK⟩\n+  intro x hx\n+  have hxs : x ∈ s := by rw [hs]; simpa using hx\n+  refine hrt x ?_\n+  rw [Metric.mem_ball, dist_eq_norm]\n+  calc ‖a x - T x‖ = ‖T x - a x‖ := by rw [norm_sub_rev]\n+    _ < ε := ha x hxs\n+    _ ≤ r x := hεle x hxs\n+\n+/-- **Finite-neighbourhood form, necessity.**  An element of the strong closure of `K` is\n+approximated by elements of `K` simultaneously on every finite set of vectors. -/\n+theorem approx_of_mem_strongClosure {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n+    (hT : T ∈ strongClosure K) (F : Finset H) (ε : ℝ) (hε : 0 < ε) :\n+    ∃ a ∈ K, ∀ x ∈ F, ‖T x - a x‖ < ε := by\n+  classical\n+  rw [strongClosure, Set.mem_setOf_eq, mem_closure_iff_nhds] at hT\n+  have hind := PointwiseConvergenceCLM.isEmbedding_coeFn (σ := RingHom.id ℂ) (E := H) (F := H)\n+  set V : Set (H → H) := Set.pi (F : Set H) (fun x => Metric.ball (T x) ε) with hV\n+  have hVnhds : V ∈ 𝓝 (fun x => T x : H → H) := by\n+    rw [nhds_pi]\n+    exact Filter.pi_mem_pi F.finite_toSet (fun x _ => Metric.ball_mem_nhds _ hε)\n+  set U : Set (StrongOperator.SOT H) := (fun B : StrongOperator.SOT H => (B : H → H)) ⁻¹' V\n+    with hU\n+  have hUnhds : U ∈ 𝓝 (StrongOperator.toSOT T) := by\n+    rw [hind.isInducing.nhds_eq_comap]\n+    exact Filter.mem_comap.2 ⟨V, hVnhds, subset_rfl⟩\n+  obtain ⟨B, hBU, hBK⟩ := hT U hUnhds\n+  refine ⟨StrongOperator.ofSOT B, hBK, fun x hx => ?_⟩\n+  have h2 := hBU x hx\n+  rw [Metric.mem_ball, dist_eq_norm] at h2\n+  rw [norm_sub_rev]\n+  exact h2\n+\n+/-- **Membership in the strong closure is exactly simultaneous finite approximation.**  This is\n+the \"arbitrary finite strong neighbourhood\" form of the closure. -/\n+theorem mem_strongClosure_iff {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {T : H →L[ℂ] H} :\n+    T ∈ strongClosure K ↔\n+      ∀ (F : Finset H) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ∃ a ∈ K, ∀ x ∈ F, ‖T x - a x‖ < ε :=\n+  ⟨fun hT F ε hε => approx_of_mem_strongClosure hT F ε hε, mem_strongClosure_of_approx⟩\n+\n+/-- Net form: the strong closure contains every strong limit of a net taken in `K`. -/\n+theorem mem_strongClosure_of_stronglyTendsto {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {ι : Type*} {l : Filter ι}\n+    [l.NeBot] {S : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)} {T : H →L[ℂ] H} (hmem : ∀ᶠ i in l, S i ∈ K)\n+    (hS : StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto l S T) : T ∈ strongClosure K := by\n+  refine mem_strongClosure_of_approx fun F ε hε => ?_\n+  have hall : ∀ᶠ i in l, ∀ x ∈ F, ‖T x - S i x‖ < ε := by\n+    refine (Filter.eventually_all_finset F).2 fun x _ => ?_\n+    have h0 : Tendsto (fun i => ‖T x - S i x‖) l (𝓝 0) := by\n+      have := (hS x).const_sub (T x)\n+      simpa using this.norm\n+    exact h0.eventually (eventually_lt_nhds hε)\n+  obtain ⟨i, hiK, hi⟩ := (hmem.and hall).exists\n+  exact ⟨S i, hiK, hi⟩\n+\n+end StrongClosure\n+\n+/-! ## Invariant subspaces and orthogonal projections -/\n+\n+section Invariant\n+\n+variable {E : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n+\n+/-- If a closed subspace `K` is invariant under `b` and under `star b`, then the orthogonal\n+projection onto `K` commutes with `b`. -/\n+theorem commute_starProjection_of_invariant (K : Submodule ℂ E) [K.HasOrthogonalProjection]\n+    (b : E →L[ℂ] E) (h1 : ∀ x ∈ K, b x ∈ K) (h2 : ∀ x ∈ K, (star b) x ∈ K) :\n+    b * K.starProjection = K.starProjection * b := by\n+  have horth : ∀ y ∈ Kᗮ, b y ∈ Kᗮ := by\n+    intro y hy\n+    rw [Submodule.mem_orthogonal]\n+    intro z hz\n+    have h : inner ℂ z (b y) = inner ℂ ((star b) z) y := by\n+      rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint, ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left]\n+    rw [h]\n+    exact (Submodule.mem_orthogonal K y).1 hy _ (h2 z hz)\n+  ext x\n+  simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply]\n+  have h3 : b (K.starProjection x) ∈ K := h1 _ (Submodule.starProjection_apply_mem K x)\n+  have h4 : b (x - K.starProjection x) ∈ Kᗮ :=\n+    horth _ (Submodule.sub_starProjection_mem_orthogonal x)\n+  have key : K.starProjection (b x)\n+      = K.starProjection (b (K.starProjection x))\n+        + K.starProjection (b (x - K.starProjection x)) := by\n+    rw [← map_add, ← map_add]\n+    congr 1\n+    abel_nf\n+  rw [key, Submodule.starProjection_eq_self_iff.2 h3,\n+    (Submodule.starProjection_apply_eq_zero_iff K).mpr h4, add_zero]\n+\n+end Invariant\n+\n+/-! ## Finite amplifications -/\n+\n+section Amplification\n+\n+variable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n+\n+/-- The `n`-fold Hilbert-space amplification `H ⊕ ⋯ ⊕ H` of `H`. -/\n+abbrev Amp (H : Type u) [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] (n : ℕ) :=\n+  PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H)\n+\n+/-- The diagonal amplification of a bounded operator. -/\n+noncomputable def ampOp (n : ℕ) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n :=\n+  (PiLp.continuousLinearEquiv 2 ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H)).symm.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L\n+    (ContinuousLinearMap.pi (fun i => T ∘L PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H) i))\n+\n+@[simp] theorem ampOp_apply (n : ℕ) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) (x : Amp H n) (i : Fin n) :\n+    (ampOp n T x) i = T (x i) := rfl\n+\n+/-- The `j`-th coordinate embedding `H → Amp H n`. -/\n+noncomputable def ampIn (n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) : H →L[ℂ] Amp H n :=\n+  (PiLp.continuousLinearEquiv 2 ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H)).symm.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L\n+    (ContinuousLinearMap.single ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H) j)\n+\n+@[simp] theorem ampIn_apply (n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) (y : H) (i : Fin n) :\n+    (ampIn n j y) i = (Pi.single j y : ∀ _ : Fin n, H) i := rfl\n+\n+theorem amp_sum_apply {n : ℕ} (s : Finset (Fin n)) (f : Fin n → Amp H n) (i : Fin n) :\n+    (∑ j ∈ s, f j) i = ∑ j ∈ s, (f j) i := by\n+  simp\n+\n+theorem amp_sub_apply {n : ℕ} (x y : Amp H n) (i : Fin n) : (x - y) i = x i - y i := rfl\n+\n+/-- Every element of `Amp H n` is the sum of its coordinate embeddings. -/\n+theorem sum_ampIn (n : ℕ) (x : Amp H n) : ∑ j, ampIn n j (x j) = x := by\n+  classical\n+  ext i\n+  rw [amp_sum_apply]\n+  simp\n+\n+theorem ampOp_one (n : ℕ) : ampOp n (1 : H →L[ℂ] H) = 1 := by ext x i; simp\n+\n+theorem ampOp_mul (n : ℕ) (S T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ampOp n (S * T) = ampOp n S * ampOp n T := by\n+  ext x i; simp\n+\n+theorem ampOp_add (n : ℕ) (S T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ampOp n (S + T) = ampOp n S + ampOp n T := by\n+  ext x i\n+  simp\n+\n+theorem ampOp_smul (n : ℕ) (c : ℂ) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ampOp n (c • T) = c • ampOp n T := by\n+  ext x i; simp\n+\n+section Complete\n+\n+variable [CompleteSpace H]\n+\n+theorem ampOp_star (n : ℕ) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ampOp n (star T) = star (ampOp n T) := by\n+  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint (ampOp n T), ContinuousLinearMap.eq_adjoint_iff]\n+  intro x y\n+  simp only [PiLp.inner_apply, ampOp_apply]\n+  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_\n+  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint, ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left]\n+\n+/-- The diagonal amplification, packaged as a unital star algebra homomorphism. -/\n+noncomputable def ampHom (n : ℕ) : (H →L[ℂ] H) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n) where\n+  toFun := ampOp n\n+  map_one' := ampOp_one n\n+  map_mul' := ampOp_mul n\n+  map_zero' := by ext x i; simp\n+  map_add' := ampOp_add n\n+  commutes' r := by\n+    have h : ampOp n ((algebraMap ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) r) = ampOp n (r • (1 : H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n+      rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]\n+    rw [h, ampOp_smul, ampOp_one, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]\n+  map_star' := ampOp_star n\n+\n+@[simp] theorem ampHom_apply (n : ℕ) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : (ampHom (H := H) n) T = ampOp n T := rfl\n+\n+end Complete\n+\n+end Amplification\n+\n+/-! ## The matrix-entry lemma -/\n+\n+section Entries\n+\n+variable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n+\n+/-- The `(i,j)` matrix entry of an operator on the amplification `Amp H n`. -/\n+noncomputable def ampEntry (n : ℕ) (S : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n) (i j : Fin n) : H →L[ℂ] H :=\n+  (PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H) i) ∘L S ∘L (ampIn n j)\n+\n+@[simp] theorem ampEntry_apply (n : ℕ) (S : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n) (i j : Fin n) (y : H) :\n+    ampEntry n S i j y = (S (ampIn n j y)) i := rfl\n+\n+theorem ampIn_comp (n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) (a : H →L[ℂ] H) (y : H) :\n+    ampIn n j (a y) = ampOp n a (ampIn n j y) := by\n+  classical\n+  ext i\n+  simp only [ampIn_apply, ampOp_apply, Pi.single_apply]\n+  split_ifs with h\n+  · rfl\n+  · simp\n+\n+/-- If `S` commutes with the amplification of every element of `A`, then each matrix entry of `S`\n+lies in the commutant of `A`. -/\n+theorem ampEntry_mem_centralizer {A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {n : ℕ} {S : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n}\n+    (hS : ∀ a ∈ A, S * ampOp n a = ampOp n a * S) (i j : Fin n) :\n+    ampEntry n S i j ∈ Set.centralizer A := by\n+  intro a ha\n+  ext y\n+  have hcomm := congrArg (fun t : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n => t (ampIn n j y)) (hS a ha)\n+  simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply] at hcomm\n+  have h1 : ampEntry n S i j (a y) = (S (ampOp n a (ampIn n j y))) i := by\n+    rw [ampEntry_apply, ampIn_comp]\n+  simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ampEntry_apply, h1, hcomm, ampOp_apply]\n+\n+/-- **Key amplification step.**  If `T` lies in the bicommutant of `A`, then its amplification\n+commutes with every operator commuting with the amplification of `A`. -/\n+theorem ampOp_commute_of_mem_bicommutant {A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n+    (hT : T ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer A)) {n : ℕ} {S : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n}\n+    (hS : ∀ a ∈ A, S * ampOp n a = ampOp n a * S) :\n+    S * ampOp n T = ampOp n T * S := by\n+  classical\n+  have hent : ∀ i j : Fin n, ampEntry n S i j * T = T * ampEntry n S i j := fun i j =>\n+    hT _ (ampEntry_mem_centralizer hS i j)\n+  ext x i\n+  simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ampOp_apply]\n+  -- expand `x` and `ampOp n T x` in coordinates\n+  have hx : x = ∑ j, ampIn n j (x j) := (sum_ampIn n x).symm\n+  have hTx : ampOp n T x = ∑ j, ampIn n j (T (x j)) := by\n+    have := sum_ampIn n (ampOp n T x)\n+    simpa using this.symm\n+  have hSx : (S x) i = ∑ j, ampEntry n S i j (x j) := by\n+    conv_lhs => rw [hx]\n+    rw [map_sum, amp_sum_apply]\n+    rfl\n+  have hSTx : (S (ampOp n T x)) i = ∑ j, ampEntry n S i j (T (x j)) := by\n+    conv_lhs => rw [hTx]\n+    rw [map_sum, amp_sum_apply]\n+    rfl\n+  rw [hSTx, hSx, map_sum]\n+  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_\n+  have h := congrArg (fun t : H →L[ℂ] H => t (x j)) (hent i j)\n+  simpa using h\n+\n+end Entries\n+\n+/-! ## The bicommutant theorem -/\n+\n+section Main\n+\n+variable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n+\n+/-- **Simultaneous approximation on a finite family of vectors.**  Every element of the\n+bicommutant of a star subalgebra `A` of `B(H)` is approximated, on any finite family of vectors\n+and to any accuracy, by an element of `A`. -/\n+theorem exists_mem_approx_on_fin (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) {T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n+    (hT : T ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))) (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → H)\n+    {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :\n+    ∃ a ∈ A, ∀ i, ‖T (v i) - a (v i)‖ < ε := by\n+  classical\n+  set ξ : Amp H n := WithLp.toLp 2 v\n+  have hξ_apply : ∀ i, ξ i = v i := fun _ => rfl\n+  -- the cyclic submodule `A ξ`\n+  set φ : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] Amp H n :=\n+    (ContinuousLinearMap.apply ℂ (Amp H n) ξ).toLinearMap ∘ₗ (ampHom n).toLinearMap\n+  set M : Submodule ℂ (Amp H n) := Submodule.map φ A.toSubmodule\n+  have hM_mem : ∀ y, y ∈ M ↔ ∃ b ∈ A, ampOp n b ξ = y := by\n+    intro y\n+    constructor\n+    · rintro ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩; exact ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩\n+    · rintro ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩; exact ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩\n+  set K : Submodule ℂ (Amp H n) := M.topologicalClosure\n+  have hKclosed : IsClosed (K : Set (Amp H n)) := M.isClosed_topologicalClosure\n+  have hKcoe : (K : Set (Amp H n)) = closure (M : Set (Amp H n)) := M.topologicalClosure_coe\n+  haveI : CompleteSpace K := hKclosed.completeSpace_coe\n+  haveI : K.HasOrthogonalProjection := inferInstance\n+  -- `ξ` belongs to the cyclic subspace, by unitality of `A`\n+  have hξK : ξ ∈ K := by\n+    refine Submodule.le_topologicalClosure M ?_\n+    refine (hM_mem ξ).2 ⟨1, A.one_mem, ?_⟩\n+    rw [ampOp_one]\n+    rfl\n+  -- the cyclic subspace is invariant under `A`\n+  have hinv : ∀ a ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ K, ampOp n a y ∈ K := by\n+    intro a ha y hy\n+    have hMmaps : Set.MapsTo (ampOp n a) (M : Set (Amp H n)) (M : Set (Amp H n)) := by\n+      intro z hz\n+      obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := (hM_mem z).1 hz\n+      refine (hM_mem _).2 ⟨a * b, mul_mem ha hb, ?_⟩\n+      rw [ampOp_mul]\n+      rfl\n+    have hmaps := hMmaps.closure (ampOp n a).continuous\n+    rw [← hKcoe] at hmaps\n+    exact hmaps (show y ∈ (K : Set (Amp H n)) from hy)\n+  -- hence the orthogonal projection onto it commutes with the amplification of `A`\n+  have hPcomm : ∀ a ∈ A, K.starProjection * ampOp n a = ampOp n a * K.starProjection := by\n+    intro a ha\n+    refine (commute_starProjection_of_invariant K (ampOp n a) (hinv a ha) ?_).symm\n+    intro y hy\n+    rw [← ampOp_star]\n+    exact hinv (star a) (star_mem ha) y hy\n+  -- and therefore with the amplification of `T`\n+  have hTcomm : K.starProjection * ampOp n T = ampOp n T * K.starProjection :=\n+    ampOp_commute_of_mem_bicommutant hT hPcomm\n+  -- so `ampOp n T ξ` lies in the cyclic subspace\n+  have hTξ : ampOp n T ξ ∈ K := by\n+    have h1 : K.starProjection ξ = ξ := Submodule.starProjection_eq_self_iff.2 hξK\n+    have h2 := congrArg (fun t : Amp H n →L[ℂ] Amp H n => t ξ) hTcomm\n+    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, h1] at h2\n+    rw [← h2]\n+    exact Submodule.starProjection_apply_mem K _\n+  -- approximate it by an element of `A ξ`\n+  have hTξ' : ampOp n T ξ ∈ closure (M : Set (Amp H n)) := by rw [← hKcoe]; exact hTξ\n+  rw [Metric.mem_closure_iff] at hTξ'\n+  obtain ⟨y, hyM, hy⟩ := hTξ' ε hε\n+  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := (hM_mem y).1 hyM\n+  refine ⟨a, ha, fun i => ?_⟩\n+  have hnorm : ‖ampOp n T ξ - ampOp n a ξ‖ < ε := by\n+    rwa [← dist_eq_norm]\n+  calc ‖T (v i) - a (v i)‖\n+      = ‖(ampOp n T ξ - ampOp n a ξ) i‖ := by\n+        rw [amp_sub_apply, ampOp_apply, ampOp_apply, hξ_apply]\n+    _ ≤ ‖ampOp n T ξ - ampOp n a ξ‖ := PiLp.norm_apply_le _ i\n+    _ < ε := hnorm\n+\n+/-- The bicommutant is contained in the strong operator closure. -/\n+theorem bicommutant_subset_strongClosure (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n+    Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n+      ⊆ strongClosure (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n+  classical\n+  intro T hT\n+  refine mem_strongClosure_of_approx fun F ε hε => ?_\n+  set e := F.equivFin\n+  obtain ⟨a, ha, hap⟩ :=\n+    exists_mem_approx_on_fin A hT F.card (fun i => ((e.symm i : F) : H)) hε\n+  refine ⟨a, ha, fun x hx => ?_⟩\n+  have hxv : x = ((e.symm (e ⟨x, hx⟩) : F) : H) := by simp\n+  have hx' := hap (e ⟨x, hx⟩)\n+  rwa [← hxv] at hx'\n+\n+/-- The strong operator closure is contained in the bicommutant. -/\n+theorem strongClosure_subset_bicommutant (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n+    strongClosure (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n+      ⊆ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :=\n+  strongClosure_subset Set.subset_centralizer_centralizer\n+    (StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_centralizer _)\n+\n+/-- **The analytic von Neumann bicommutant (double commutant) theorem.**\n+\n+For a unital complex star subalgebra `A` of the bounded operators on a complex Hilbert space `H`\n+(unitality is automatic for `StarSubalgebra ℂ _`), the strong operator closure of `A` coincides\n+with its bicommutant `A''`. -/\n+theorem strongClosure_eq_bicommutant (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n+    strongClosure (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n+      = Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :=\n+  Set.Subset.antisymm (strongClosure_subset_bicommutant A) (bicommutant_subset_strongClosure A)\n+\n+/-- The same statement phrased with the concrete von Neumann algebra `A''` produced by the\n+algebraic bicommutant core of `P49A`'s companion file. -/\n+theorem strongClosure_eq_vonNeumannGenerated (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n+    strongClosure (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n+      = (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n+  rw [strongClosure_eq_bicommutant, StarSubalgebra.coe_vonNeumannGenerated]\n+\n+/-- A concrete von Neumann algebra is exactly the strong operator closure of itself; equivalently,\n+a strongly closed unital star subalgebra equals its own bicommutant. -/\n+theorem strongClosure_eq_self_iff (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n+    strongClosure (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ↔\n+      ∃ M : VonNeumannAlgebra H, (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n+  constructor\n+  · intro h\n+    refine ⟨StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A, ?_⟩\n+    rw [← strongClosure_eq_vonNeumannGenerated, h]\n+  · rintro ⟨M, hM⟩\n+    rw [strongClosure_eq_bicommutant, ← hM, M.centralizer_centralizer]\n+\n+end Main\n+\n+end VonNeumannBicommutant\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
